Synthesis
  Tetration does what the ladder predicts qualitatively: it is the hyper-lacunary edge of the speed spectrum, with low H-entropy and a positive sampled cascade.
  The finite modulus still matters: towers fold modulo the sampling denominators, so a tetration family can reduce entropy without automatically maximizing the product. It is best read as the decorrelation extreme whose remaining obstructions are aliasing events.
  Best sampled product: L3_geom2; lowest mean H-entropy: L4_tetr3.
  Cascade product = repeated multiplication of runner clearances; the proof target is to show finite aliasing cannot create an AP-like zero factor outside the additive/tight regime.
